<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Zelos final-round defense</title>
<meta name="description" content="Zelos: evidence-gated QC for organ-on-a-chip images. Final-round defense deck, v1.1.">
<style>
:root{
  --bg:#fbfbfd; --fg:#1d1d1f; --mut:#6e6e73; --faint:#d2d2d7; --surf:#f2f2f5; --acc:#0071e3;
  --good:#1a7f37; --bad:#c62828; --warn:#b45309; --track:#e6e6eb; --cause:#7a7a85;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){
  :root{
    --bg:#000; --fg:#f5f5f7; --mut:#a1a1a6; --faint:#3a3a3c; --surf:#1c1c1e; --acc:#2997ff;
    --good:#30d158; --bad:#ff6961; --warn:#ffb340; --track:#2c2c2e; --cause:#8e8e93;
  }
}
*{box-sizing:border-box}
html,body{height:100%;margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);overflow:hidden;
  font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"SF Pro Display","SF Pro Text","Segoe UI",Roboto,"Helvetica Neue",Arial,"Noto Sans",sans-serif;
  -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;text-rendering:optimizeLegibility}
#deck{position:absolute;left:50%;top:50%;width:1920px;height:1080px;margin:-540px 0 0 -960px;
  transform-origin:center center;transform:translateY(var(--dy,0px)) scale(var(--s,1))}
.slide{position:absolute;inset:0;padding:74px 140px 92px;display:none;flex-direction:column;background:var(--bg)}
.slide.on{display:flex}
h1,h2,h3,p,ul,figure{margin:0}
.eyebrow{font-size:26px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.09em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--acc);margin-bottom:16px}
h2{font-size:72px;line-height:1.05;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.025em;max-width:1500px}
h2 .dim{color:var(--mut)}
.mega{font-size:300px;line-height:.95;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.05em}
.lead{font-size:76px;line-height:1.1;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;margin-top:30px}
.sub{font-size:40px;line-height:1.35;color:var(--mut);margin-top:34px;max-width:1380px}
.meta{position:absolute;left:140px;bottom:96px;font-size:28px;color:var(--mut)}
p.body{font-size:40px;line-height:1.38;color:var(--mut);max-width:1500px;margin-top:30px}
.note{font-size:26px;line-height:1.4;color:var(--mut);margin-top:auto;max-width:1640px}
.note b{color:var(--fg);font-weight:600}
.cols{display:grid;gap:56px;margin-top:40px;align-items:start}
.c2{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}
.c3{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}
.split{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,900px) minmax(0,1fr)}
.cols>*{min-width:0}
.card{background:var(--surf);border-radius:30px;padding:36px 40px}
.card h3{font-size:38px;font-weight:650;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin-bottom:12px}
.card p{font-size:30px;line-height:1.38;color:var(--mut)}
.stat{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;padding:18px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--faint)}
.stat:first-child{border-top:0}
.stat .n{font-size:92px;line-height:1;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.04em}
.stat .l{font-size:30px;line-height:1.3;color:var(--mut)}
.stat.good .n{color:var(--good)} .stat.bad .n{color:var(--bad)} .stat.acc .n{color:var(--acc)}
.delta{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto;gap:8px 36px;align-items:baseline;margin-top:24px}
.delta .l{font-size:30px;color:var(--fg)}
.delta .v{font-size:42px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em;white-space:nowrap}
.delta .v i{font-style:normal;color:var(--mut);font-weight:500;padding:0 14px}
.delta .v .a{color:var(--bad)} .delta .v .b{color:var(--good)}
.tiles{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:28px;margin-top:36px}
.tile{background:var(--surf);border-radius:28px;padding:28px 34px}
.tile .n{font-size:76px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.04em;line-height:1;color:var(--good)}
.tile .l{font-size:28px;color:var(--mut);margin-top:8px;line-height:1.3}
table.t{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:28px}
table.t th{text-align:left;font-weight:600;color:var(--mut);font-size:23px;letter-spacing:.02em;padding:10px 14px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--faint)}
table.t td{padding:10px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--faint);white-space:nowrap}
table.t td:first-child{white-space:normal}
table.t tr.hl td{font-weight:650;color:var(--fg)}
table.t tr.hl td:first-child{color:var(--acc)}
table.t.sm{font-size:25px}
table.t.sm td{padding:8px 14px}
table.t.wrap td{white-space:normal;vertical-align:top;font-size:27px;line-height:1.3;padding:16px 18px}
table.t.wrap td:first-child{width:250px;font-weight:650}
table.t.wrap td:last-child{width:230px;color:var(--mut)}
table.t.sm th{font-size:21px}
.cap{font-size:25px;color:var(--mut);margin:10px 0 8px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.01em}
ul.pts{list-style:none;padding:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px}
ul.pts li{font-size:32px;line-height:1.34;padding-left:30px;position:relative;color:var(--fg)}
ul.pts li::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:0;top:.6em;width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--acc)}
ul.pts li.w::before{background:var(--warn)} ul.pts li.b::before{background:var(--bad)} ul.pts li.g::before{background:var(--good)}
ul.pts li small{display:block;font-size:26px;color:var(--mut);margin-top:4px}
.callout{border-left:8px solid var(--warn);background:var(--surf);border-radius:0 24px 24px 0;padding:26px 34px;font-size:30px;line-height:1.36;margin-top:26px}
.callout b{font-weight:650}
.callout.b{border-color:var(--bad)} .callout.a{border-color:var(--acc)}
/* certificates */
.certs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:36px;margin-top:26px}
figure.cert{background:var(--surf);border-radius:30px;padding:24px;overflow:hidden;border-top:8px solid var(--faint)}
figure.cert.fail{border-top-color:var(--bad)} figure.cert.pass{border-top-color:var(--good)}
figure.cert img{display:block;width:100%;height:200px;object-fit:cover;border-radius:18px;filter:saturate(.9)}
figure.cert figcaption{padding:14px 8px 0;font-size:24px;line-height:1.3}
.cert .head{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:20px;margin-bottom:8px}
.chip{font-size:30px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.04em;border-radius:12px;padding:3px 18px;color:#fff}
.chip.fail{background:var(--bad)} .chip.pass{background:var(--good)} .chip.review{background:var(--warn)}
.cert .score{font-size:28px;color:var(--mut)}
.cert .row{display:flex;gap:14px}.cert .k{color:var(--mut);min-width:104px;font-weight:600;font-size:23px;letter-spacing:.03em;text-transform:uppercase;padding-top:2px}
.cert .basis{color:var(--warn);margin:6px 0 2px;font-size:23px}
.cert .ev{margin-top:4px;font-size:23px}.cert .ev .id{color:var(--mut);margin-left:10px;font-size:21px}
.cert .ledger{margin-top:8px;font-size:23px}
.cert .ledger ul{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:4px 0 0}
.cert .ledger li{color:var(--mut);font-size:21px;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
.cert .tick{color:var(--good);margin-right:10px;font-weight:700}
.cert .cap{margin:0 0 8px;font-weight:500;font-size:22px}
/* charts */
svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}
svg text{font-family:inherit;fill:var(--fg)}
svg .lab{font-size:25px;fill:var(--fg)} svg .val{font-size:25px;font-weight:650;fill:var(--fg)} svg .val.small{font-size:19px;fill:var(--mut);font-weight:500}
svg .track{fill:var(--track)} svg .det{fill:var(--acc)} svg .miss{fill:var(--bad)} svg .cause{fill:var(--cause)}
svg .good{fill:var(--good)} svg .bad{fill:var(--bad)} svg .test{fill:var(--acc)}
svg .missl{fill:var(--bad);font-weight:650} svg .okl{fill:var(--good)}
svg .target{stroke:var(--warn);stroke-width:3;stroke-dasharray:10 8} svg .axis{stroke:var(--faint);stroke-width:2}
.legend{display:flex;gap:34px;font-size:24px;color:var(--mut);margin-bottom:14px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.legend span::before{content:"";display:inline-block;width:22px;height:14px;border-radius:4px;margin-right:10px;vertical-align:-1px;background:var(--acc)}
.legend .t::before{background:none;border-top:4px dashed var(--warn);height:0;border-radius:0;width:30px;vertical-align:4px}
.legend .c::before{background:var(--cause)} .legend .m::before{background:var(--bad)} .legend .g::before{background:var(--good)}
/* arch + tiles */
.grid6{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:28px;margin-top:40px}
.grid6 .card{min-height:300px}
.grid6 .card h3{font-size:36px}
.links{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:20px 40px;margin-top:56px;font-size:36px;align-items:baseline}
.links .k{color:var(--mut);font-size:27px;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:600}
.links .u{font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em}
.road{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:28px;margin-top:44px}
.road .card{min-height:250px}
.road .tag{font-size:23px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--acc);margin-bottom:12px}
/* HUD */
#hud{position:fixed;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;height:3px;background:transparent}
#bar{height:3px;background:var(--acc);width:0;transition:width .25s ease}
#count{position:fixed;right:22px;bottom:14px;font-size:15px;color:var(--mut);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;letter-spacing:.04em;z-index:5}
#brand{position:fixed;left:22px;bottom:14px;font-size:15px;color:var(--mut);letter-spacing:.04em;z-index:5}
#notes{position:fixed;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;display:none;max-height:30vh;overflow:auto;padding:18px 7vw 40px;
  background:var(--surf);border-top:1px solid var(--faint);font-size:19px;line-height:1.5;z-index:6}
#notes b{color:var(--acc);letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:13px}
body.notes #notes{display:block}
.slide aside.notes{display:none}
@media (max-width:900px){ #notes{font-size:15px} }
/* print: one slide per page */
@page{size:1920px 1080px;margin:0}
@media print{
  html,body{height:auto;overflow:visible;background:#fff}
  #deck{position:static;margin:0;width:1920px;height:auto;transform:none}
  .slide,.slide.on{display:flex;position:relative;inset:auto;width:1920px;height:1080px;break-after:page;page-break-after:always;overflow:hidden}
  #hud,#bar,#count,#brand,#notes{display:none!important}
}
html.print,html.print body{height:auto;overflow:visible}
html.print #deck{position:static;margin:0;width:1920px;height:auto;transform:none}
html.print .slide,html.print .slide.on{display:flex;position:relative;inset:auto;width:1920px;height:1080px;overflow:hidden;border-bottom:2px solid var(--faint)}
html.print #hud,html.print #bar,html.print #count,html.print #brand,html.print #notes{display:none!important}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<!-- Generated by scripts/build_defense_kit.py from results/*.json at commit {{git_sha}} ({{date}}). Do not edit by hand. -->
<main id="deck">

<!-- 1 -->
<section class="slide" data-title="Title">
  <div class="eyebrow">AI4S Open Innovation &middot; AI for Life Science &middot; Final round</div>
  <h1 class="mega">Zelos</h1>
  <p class="lead">Every organ-on-a-chip image, certified.</p>
  <p class="sub">An evidence-gated QC agent. It finds the imaging fault, names the lab fix, cites open literature, and blocks every claim the evidence cannot support.</p>
  <div class="meta">Philip Simon Derock &middot; v1.1 final-round build &middot; Research tool, not a medical device</div>
  <aside class="notes">Hello, I am Philip, and this is Zelos. In one sentence: Zelos looks at an organ-on-a-chip image, tells you whether you can trust it, says what went wrong and what to do about it, and refuses to say anything its evidence cannot back up. I will show you what works, what does not, and what I corrected since the submission.</aside>
</section>

<!-- 2 -->
<section class="slide" data-title="The problem">
  <div class="eyebrow">The problem</div>
  <h2>Images become datasets. Datasets become digital twins.</h2>
  <div class="cols c2" style="margin-top:56px">
    <div class="card"><h3>Bad frames corrupt data silently</h3><p>A defocused, saturated, vignetted or bubble-filled frame looks like any other file. Once it is in a dataset, nobody knows it is there.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Invented evidence corrupts decisions silently</h3><p>A language model asked to explain a bad frame can invent a number or a citation, and it sounds just as confident when it does.</p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="body">Labs image hundreds of frames per experiment and cannot review them all. The question is not whether to automate the check, but whether the check can be trusted.</p>
  <aside class="notes">Organ-on-a-chip labs image their cultures every day, and those images become datasets and, increasingly, inputs to digital twins. A bad frame does not announce itself, and neither does a language model that makes up a citation. Both fail silently, and both end up inside the asset. So the check has to be automatic and it has to be auditable.</aside>
</section>

<!-- 3 -->
<section class="slide" data-title="The certificate">
  <div class="eyebrow">What Zelos outputs</div>
  <h2>Every image gets a certificate.</h2>
  <div class="certs">
    {{html.card_fail}}
    {{html.card_pass}}
  </div>
  <div class="note"><b>Verdict, route, cause, lab action, cited basis, claim ledger.</b> Real pipeline output (web/public/data/site.json); images from Movcana et al., Data 2024, shared under CC BY / CC BY-SA. The FAIL frame is an injected fault on a real image; the cited passage is retrieved context, and the rule's own literature basis is shown as the amber line.</div>
  <aside class="notes">This is what comes out: a verdict, a route that says what to do next, the named cause, the lab action, the passage it cites, and a ledger that lists every sentence with the tool output or passage behind it. On the left is a real image where I injected a severity-{{sev.top}} over-exposure, and Zelos fails it and names the cause. On the right is an untouched real image that passes. The amber line on the left is deliberate: for that cause our corpus does not support the action, and the certificate says so.</aside>
</section>

<!-- 4 -->
<section class="slide" data-title="Architecture">
  <div class="eyebrow">Architecture</div>
  <h2>The LLM proposes.<br>Tools compute.<br>The gate disposes.</h2>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 1640 330" role="img" aria-label="Pipeline: image, physics QC, cause and action, evidence retrieval, LLM explainer, grounding gate, certificate" style="margin-top:30px">
    <g font-size="24">
      <rect x="0" y="20" width="210" height="230" rx="22" fill="var(--surf)"/>
      <text x="105" y="125" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="650" font-size="27">Brightfield</text><text x="105" y="162" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--mut)">image</text>

      <rect x="238" y="20" width="210" height="230" rx="22" fill="var(--surf)" stroke="var(--acc)" stroke-width="3"/>
      <text x="343" y="76" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="650" font-size="27">Physics QC</text>
      <text x="343" y="122" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--mut)">{{n_metrics}} metrics</text>
      <text x="343" y="160" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--mut)">z vs session</text>
      <text x="343" y="198" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--mut)">0 LLM calls</text>

      <rect x="476" y="20" width="210" height="230" rx="22" fill="var(--surf)" stroke="var(--acc)" stroke-width="3"/>
      <text x="581" y="76" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="650" font-size="27">Cause + action</text>
      <text x="581" y="122" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--mut)">signatures</text>
      <text x="581" y="160" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--mut)">fixed rule table</text>
      <text x="581" y="198" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--mut)">route</text>

      <rect x="714" y="20" width="210" height="230" rx="22" fill="var(--surf)" stroke="var(--acc)" stroke-width="3"/>
      <text x="819" y="76" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="650" font-size="27">Evidence</text>
      <text x="819" y="122" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--mut)">Cohere + Qdrant</text>
      <text x="819" y="160" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--mut)">BM25 + rerank</text>
      <text x="819" y="198" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--mut)">abstains</text>

      <rect x="952" y="20" width="210" height="230" rx="22" fill="var(--surf)" stroke="var(--warn)" stroke-width="3"/>
      <text x="1057" y="76" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="650" font-size="27">LLM explainer</text>
      <text x="1057" y="122" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--mut)">typed claims</text>
      <text x="1057" y="160" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--mut)">max {{agent.max_calls}} calls</text>
      <text x="1057" y="198" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--mut)">swappable</text>

      <rect x="1190" y="20" width="210" height="230" rx="22" fill="var(--surf)" stroke="var(--good)" stroke-width="3"/>
      <text x="1295" y="76" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="650" font-size="27">Gate</text>
      <text x="1295" y="122" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--mut)">numbers match</text>
      <text x="1295" y="160" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--mut)">citations support</text>
      <text x="1295" y="198" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--mut)">repair, then block</text>

      <rect x="1428" y="20" width="212" height="230" rx="22" fill="var(--fg)"/>
      <text x="1534" y="125" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="650" font-size="27" style="fill:var(--bg)">Certificate</text>
      <text x="1534" y="162" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--bg)">+ claim ledger</text>
    </g>
    <g stroke="var(--mut)" stroke-width="3" fill="none">
      <path d="M212 135 H236"/><path d="M450 135 H474"/><path d="M688 135 H712"/><path d="M926 135 H950"/><path d="M1164 135 H1188"/><path d="M1402 135 H1426"/>
    </g>
    <g stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round">
      <path d="M244 282 H918" stroke="var(--acc)"/><path d="M958 282 H1156" stroke="var(--warn)"/><path d="M1196 282 H1394" stroke="var(--good)"/>
    </g>
    <g font-size="26" font-weight="700">
      <text x="581" y="322" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--acc)">TOOLS COMPUTE</text>
      <text x="1057" y="322" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--warn)">LLM PROPOSES</text>
      <text x="1295" y="322" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--good)">GATE DISPOSES</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <div class="note">The verdict, cause and action never depend on the LLM. If the model is wrong, slow or absent, the certificate is still correct; it is only less fluent.</div>
  <aside class="notes">The design rule is the headline: the physics tools compute the verdict, the cause and the action with no language model involved, and the model only proposes sentences as typed claims, in at most {{agent.max_calls}} calls. A deterministic gate then checks every number against a tool output and every citation against a retrieved passage, repairs once, and blocks what it cannot support. That is why the model is swappable, and I will show you that it is.</aside>
</section>

<!-- 5 -->
<section class="slide" data-title="Result A: trust layer">
  <div class="eyebrow">Result A &middot; the trust layer</div>
  <h2>The gate caught every fabrication.</h2>
  <div class="cols" style="grid-template-columns:minmax(0,800px) minmax(0,1fr);margin-top:26px">
    <div>
      <div class="tiles" style="margin-top:0">
        <div class="tile"><div class="n">{{gate.caught}}</div><div class="l">injected fabrications blocked</div></div>
        <div class="tile"><div class="n">{{gate.false_block}}</div><div class="l">correct claims wrongly blocked</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="delta">
        <div class="l">Unsupported claims in LLM answers</div><div class="v"><span class="a">{{e5.unsup_un}}</span><i>&rarr;</i><span class="b">{{e5.unsup_g}}</span></div>
        <div class="l">Valid citations</div><div class="v"><span class="a">{{e5.cite_un}}</span><i>&rarr;</i><span class="b">{{e5.cite_g}}</span></div>
        <div class="l">Unsafe adversarial outputs</div><div class="v"><span class="a">{{e5.unsafe_un}}</span><i>&rarr;</i><span class="b">{{e5.unsafe_g}}</span></div>
        <div class="l">Abstention recall</div><div class="v"><span class="a">{{e5.abst_rec_un}}</span><i>&rarr;</i><span class="b">{{e5.abst_rec_g}}</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="cap">Same gate, {{sweep.n_models_ok}} LLMs (n={{sweep.n}} QC explanations)</div>
      {{html.table_sweep}}
      <div class="callout a"><b>Bigger models did not help.</b> {{sweep.best_name}} gives the most supported claims per case ({{sweep.best.per_case}}) at {{sweep.best.cost}} per 100 answers; the dearest model costs {{sweep.dearest_cost}} and supports fewer.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="note"><b>Read with care.</b> Fabrications: {{gate.n_kinds}} kinds, {{gate.per_kind_n}} each (fake numbers, fake citations, wrong support, uncited literature, orphan inferences). Without the gate: {{e5.unsup_un_k}} claims unsupported, {{e5.unsafe_un_k}} adversarial outputs unsafe. After the gate the rate is zero by construction, so the fault-injection test is the real test of the gate. Support checks are lexical: a weak test of meaning.</div>
  <aside class="notes">First result, the trust layer: we injected {{gate.caught_n}} fabrications of {{gate.n_kinds}} kinds and the gate caught {{gate.caught}}, while blocking {{gate.false_block}} correct claims. On real model outputs the unsupported claim rate falls from {{e5.unsup_un}} to {{e5.unsup_g}} and unsafe adversarial outputs from {{e5.unsafe_un}} to {{e5.unsafe_g}}, and because the gate does the checking we could swap in {{sweep.n_others}} larger models, none of which beat the small one. The caveat is that the after-gate rate is zero by construction and the support test is lexical, so it is a weak test of meaning.</aside>
</section>

<!-- 6 -->
<section class="slide" data-title="Result B: known faults">
  <div class="eyebrow">Result B &middot; faults with known ground truth</div>
  <h2>Found, and named. With honest misses.</h2>
  <div class="cols" style="grid-template-columns:560px 1fr;margin-top:30px">
    <div>
      <div class="stat acc"><div class="n">{{e1.batch.det3}}</div><div class="l">of severity {{sev.mid}} and {{sev.top}} faults flagged, with {{e1.batch.clean}} of clean images flagged</div></div>
      <div class="stat good"><div class="n">{{e1.batch.sig}}</div><div class="l">cause named correctly among flagged faults; chance is {{e1.chance}}</div></div>
      <div class="callout b" style="margin-top:14px"><b>Mostly missed even at severity {{sev.mid}}:</b> {{miss_list_detail}}.</div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="legend"><span>Detected at severity {{sev.mid}}</span><span class="m">Mostly missed</span><span class="c">Cause named, of flagged</span></div>
      {{html.kind_chart}}
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="note">{{n_base}} real test-session images &times; {{n_kinds}} fault kinds &times; severities {{n_sev_list}}. Session-relative reference. Cutoffs calibrated to at most {{target_ff}} false flags on expert-good calibration sessions; cause signatures fitted on {{n_sig}} development images. The faults are ours: this benchmark checks sensitivity, not clinical relevance.</div>
  <aside class="notes">Second result, where we know the right answer because we injected the fault. At a threshold calibrated to flag {{e1.batch.clean}} of clean images, Zelos catches {{e1.batch.det3}} of the severity {{sev.mid}} and {{sev.top}} faults and names the right cause {{e1.batch.sig}} of the time, against {{e1.chance}} by chance. The red bars are the honest part: {{miss_list}} are mostly missed even at severity {{sev.mid}}. The benchmark is ours, so it shows sensitivity to these faults, not that they are the ones that matter most in a lab.</aside>
</section>

<!-- 7 -->
<section class="slide" data-title="Result C: head to head">
  <div class="eyebrow">Result C &middot; head to head</div>
  <h2>Head to head on the same faults.</h2>
  <div class="cols" style="grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1020px) minmax(0,1fr);margin-top:26px">
    <div>
      <div class="cap">Injected faults (severity {{sev.mid}} and {{sev.top}}); each system calibrated to at most {{target_ff}} false alarms</div>
      {{html.table_h2h}}
      <div class="cap" style="margin-top:26px">Vision LLMs, one prompt, n={{vlm.n}} per group, same images</div>
      {{html.table_vlm}}
    </div>
    <ul class="pts" style="gap:16px">
      <li>The head uses the same session-averaged false-alarm rule. One approach family, implemented by us, not any team's model.</li>
      <li class="w">It learns the expert label, not faults, and cannot name a cause.</li>
      <li class="w">Vision LLMs find more severe faults ({{vlm.det5_min}} to {{vlm.det5_max}} vs {{vlm.zelos.det5}}) but flag {{vlm.ff_clean_min}} to {{vlm.ff_clean_max}} of clean images.</li>
      <li class="b">One model gave no parsable reply on {{vlm.unparsed_cases}} cases: reported, not dropped.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="note">On the expert label itself, the same head reaches AUROC {{e2.head.auroc}} against {{e2.qc_batch.auroc}} for the Zelos artifact score (next slide). Different task, different winner.</div>
  <aside class="notes">Third result: a head-to-head against a linear head on frozen DINOv2 embeddings trained on the expert label, which is the approach family many entries use, calibrated to the same false-alarm rule as Zelos. On the injected faults it finds {{h2h.det3}} where Zelos finds {{e1.batch.det3}}, and it cannot say what is wrong. Vision language models find more of the severe faults but flag {{vlm.ff_clean_min}} to {{vlm.ff_clean_max}} of clean images, and the caveats are that the head is my implementation, the language models got one prompt, and there are only {{vlm.n}} images per group.</aside>
</section>

<!-- 8 -->
<section class="slide" data-title="Result D: the shift finding">
  <div class="eyebrow">Result D &middot; the shift finding</div>
  <h2>Absolute thresholds do not transfer between imaging sessions.</h2>
  <div class="cols split" style="margin-top:30px">
    <div>
      <div class="legend"><span class="g">Unseen-session estimate, within target</span><span class="m">above target</span><span>Test sessions</span><span class="t">Target</span></div>
      {{html.shift_chart}}
    </div>
    <ul class="pts">
      <li class="b">Calibrated absolute cutoffs miss the {{target_ff}} false-alarm target across unseen sessions: {{cal.pooled.loso}} and {{cal.between.loso}}. Session-relative scoring meets it: {{cal.batch.loso}}.</li>
      <li class="w">In the upper fifth of sessions single-image scoring flags {{cal.between.p80}} of good images, session-relative {{cal.batch.p80}}.</li>
      <li>On the {{n_test_sessions}} test sessions the absolute modes were conservative ({{op.between.ff}} false flags) and found only {{op.between.recall}} of expert-bad images. The pre-registered z={{prereg_z}} rule flags {{op.pooled.z3}} of expert-good.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="note"><b>So Zelos scores each image against its own imaging session.</b> Single-image mode remains available, and it is the weaker mode.</div>
  <aside class="notes">This is the finding that changed the design: fixed thresholds do not transfer across imaging sessions. When we leave one whole session out, the absolute cutoffs flag {{cal.pooled.loso}} and {{cal.between.loso}} of good images against a {{target_ff}} target, and in the worst fifth of sessions it is {{cal.between.p80}}. Scoring each image relative to its own session gives {{cal.batch.loso}}, which is why the session-relative mode is the default and single-image mode is the weaker option.</aside>
</section>

<!-- 9 -->
<section class="slide" data-title="The expert label">
  <div class="eyebrow">What the expert label measures</div>
  <h2>The expert label tracks culture state, not image faults.</h2>
  <div class="cols split" style="margin-top:30px">
    <div>
      <div class="cap">Agreement with the expert label: {{n_test}} images, {{n_test_sessions}} held-out sessions</div>
