      <li class="g">A kNN lookup against expert-labelled neighbours reaches {{e2.knn_dino.auroc}} {{e2.knn_dino.ci}}; within the same imaging day {{e2.knn_dino.within}}. Zelos reports this as a separate culture-state output.</li>
      <li class="b">Other entries report higher expert-label AUROC than Zelos's artifact score. We do not claim to beat them. Zelos answers a different question: is this frame technically sound?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <aside class="notes">An honest slide. Against the expert good-or-bad label the artifact score is at chance, {{e2.qc_batch.auroc}}, while a lookup against expert-labelled neighbours reaches {{e2.knn_dino.auroc}}, so the label tracks the state of the culture and not the quality of the image. Other entries report higher expert-label scores than our artifact score and we do not claim to beat them; Zelos reports the culture-state signal as a second output and answers a different question, which is whether you can trust this frame.</aside>
</section>

